  is pre-existing base code, not the merge mechanism:
    $ venv/bin/python -c "from logging.config import fileConfig; from alembic.config import Config; \
        import logging; l=logging.getLogger('app.api.v1.health'); print('before', l.disabled); \
        fileConfig(Config('alembic.ini').config_file_name); print('after', l.disabled)"
    before disabled= False level= 0 propagate= True
    after  disabled= True level= 0 propagate= True
  alembic/env.py:20 calls fileConfig(...) with default disable_existing_loggers=True, which globally
  disables `app.api.v1.health`; migration tests run earlier in the suite, so the new test's caplog sees
  nothing. Reported as a finding, not a pass and not a hidden failure.

